{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792482400641,"sessionID":"ses_ea7b94584ffejNtLbskOVKVBz0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_f830e32a54c246c7a0363127","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"D:\\firmware-test\\experiments\\2026-10-20-qwen38-27b-harness-comparison\\runs\\run-20261020-154440-282906\\tasks\\opencode__spi-i2c-002__1\\131cd7df\\workspace\\task.md"},"output":"<path>D:\\firmware-test\\experiments\\2026-10-20-qwen38-27b-harness-comparison\\runs\\run-20261020-154440-282906\\tasks\\opencode__spi-i2c-002__1\\131cd7df\\workspace\\task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: Write a Zephyr RTOS application that performs an SPI loopback test.\n2: \n3: Requirements:\n4: 1. Get the SPI bus device using DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))\n5: 2. Verify the device is initialized and ready before use\n6: 3. Define a transmit buffer of 8 bytes initialized with a known pattern (e.g., 0x01 through 0x08)\n7: 4. Define a receive buffer of 8 bytes initialized to zero\n8: 5. Configure struct spi_config with frequency 1000000, operation SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)\n9: 6. Set up struct spi_buf for tx and rx, each pointing to their respective buffers with len = 8\n10: 7. Set up struct spi_buf_set for tx_bufs and rx_bufs, each with buf pointer and count = 1\n11: 8. Call spi_transceive() with the spi_config, tx_bufs, and rx_bufs\n12: 9. Check the return value for errors; print error and return on failure\n13: 10. Compare transmit and receive buffers byte-by-byte to verify loopback\n14: 11. Print \"SPI loopback successful\" on match, \"SPI loopback mismatch\" on failure\n15: \n16: Use the Zephyr SPI API: spi_transceive, struct spi_config, struct spi_buf, struct spi_buf_set.\n17: \n18: Include proper headers: zephyr/kernel.h, zephyr/device.h, zephyr/drivers/spi.h, string.h.\n19: \n20: Output ONLY the complete C source file.\n21: \n22: \n23: Submission instruction: write the complete C source to submission/main.c using file tools instead of returning it in chat. Do not access paths outside this task workspace.\n\n(End of file - total 23 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"Write a Zephyr RTOS application that performs an SPI loopback test.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Get the SPI bus device using DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))\n2. Verify the device is initialized and ready before use\n3. Define a transmit buffer of 8 bytes initialized with a known pattern (e.g., 0x01 through 0x08)\n4. Define a receive buffer of 8 bytes initialized to zero\n5. Configure struct spi_config with frequency 1000000, operation SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)\n6. Set up struct spi_buf for tx and rx, each pointing to their respective buffers with len = 8\n7. Set up struct spi_buf_set for tx_bufs and rx_bufs, each with buf pointer and count = 1\n8. Call spi_transceive() with the spi_config, tx_bufs, and rx_bufs\n9. Check the return value for errors; print error and return on failure\n10. Compare transmit and receive buffers byte-by-byte to verify loopback\n11. Print \"SPI loopback successful\" on match, \"SPI loopback mismatch\" on failure\n\nUse the Zephyr SPI API: spi_transceive, struct spi_config, struct spi_buf, struct spi_buf_set.\n\nInclude proper headers: zephyr/kernel.h, zephyr/device.h, zephyr/drivers/spi.h, string.h.\n\nOutput ONLY the complete C source file.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"D:\\firmware-test\\experiments\\2026-10-20-qwen38-27b-harness-comparison\\runs\\run-20261020-154440-282906\\tasks\\opencode__spi-i2c-002__1\\131cd7df\\workspace\\task.md","text":"Write a Zephyr RTOS application that performs an SPI loopback test.\n\nRequirements:\n1. Get the SPI bus device using DEVICE_DT_GET(DT_NODELABEL(spi0))\n2. Verify the device is initialized and ready before use\n3. Define a transmit buffer of 8 bytes initialized with a known pattern (e.g., 0x01 through 0x08)\n4. Define a receive buffer of 8 bytes initialized to zero\n5. Configure struct spi_config with frequency 1000000, operation SPI_OP_MODE_MASTER | SPI_WORD_SET(8)\n6. Set up struct spi_buf for tx and rx, each pointing to their respective buffers with len = 8\n7. Set up struct spi_buf_set for tx_bufs and rx_bufs, each with buf pointer and count = 1\n8. Call spi_transceive() with the spi_config, tx_bufs, and rx_bufs\n9. Check the return value for errors; print error and return on failure\n10. Compare transmit and receive buffers byte-by-byte to verify loopback\n11. Print \"SPI loopback successful\" on match, \"SPI loopback mismatch\" on failure\n\nUse the Zephyr SPI API: spi_transceive, struct spi_config, struct spi_buf, struct spi_buf_set.\n\nInclude proper headers: zephyr/kernel.h, zephyr/device.h, zephyr/drivers/spi.h, string.h.\n\nOutput ONLY the complete C source file.\n\n\nSubmission instruction: write the complete C source to submission/main.c using file tools instead of returning it in chat. Do not access paths outside this task workspace.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":23,"totalLines":23,"truncated":false}},"title":"firmware-test\\experiments\\2026-10-20-qwen38-27b-harness-comparison\\runs\\run-20261020-154440-282906\\tasks\\opencode__spi-i2c-002__1\\131cd7df\\workspace\\task.md","time":{"start":1792482400611,"end":1792482400637}},"metadata":{"anthropic":{"caller":{"type":"direct"}}},"id":"prt_15846d819001NYpk5IDeRcZALJ","sessionID":"ses_ea7b94584ffejNtLbskOVKVBz0","messageID":"msg_15846d3be001DgwmtfAqawJSfn"}}
